# Tasks: {{title}}

## Target State

Implement the complete approved behavior for `{{change_id}}`, not a partial
delivery. Use the capability slices below as independently verifiable technical
checkpoints; OpenSpec remains the canonical plan.

## Critical Path

- List the dependency-ordered tasks that directly satisfy the Completion
  Contract and keep optional hardening outside that path.

## Incidental Finding Budget

- Permit only a bounded minimal guard inside the approved contract and write
  set. Record every deferred or blocked finding in the `TASK_LEDGER.md`
  Incidental Finding Register; the register does not authorize follow-up work.

## Escalation Triggers (Authority Delta)

- Resolve every deviation through the centralized authority-delta seam. Ask the
  human only for non-empty concrete `missingAuthority`; repairable evidence or
  validation drift uses `FAIL_CLOSED_REPAIR`, not awaiting state.
- A material expansion of scope, authority, dependency, schema, migration,
  public behavior, external target/effect, destructive risk, or write set is a
  Human Gate only when the approved contract does not already cover it.
- Required behavior and failing acceptance criteria remain on the Critical
  Path and may not be deferred.

## Completion Contract

- [ ] Target State is implemented.
- [ ] Every Capability Slice is done or blocked with a recorded reason.
- [ ] Acceptance Criteria are checked.
- [ ] Validation Commands have been run or documented as unavailable.
- [ ] Verification evidence is recorded.
- [ ] Workflow state is updated.
- [ ] Any applicable project-directed implementation-readiness Requirement has
  a current Ready receipt and independent ordinary authority before product
  mutation.
- [ ] Any automatic external-effect chain has a predeclared Standing Milestone
  External Effects Contract bound to exact identities, evidence, exclusions,
  failure policy, and reentry policy.

## Continuation Policy

- Execution policy: `auto-until-terminal`.
- After each item, return evidence to `project-orchestrator` and derive
  `CONTINUE_NEXT_ITEM`, `CHECKPOINT_AND_CONTINUE`,
  `VERIFY_ACTIVE_CHANGE`, `AWAIT_HUMAN`, `READY_FOR_EXTERNAL_EFFECT`, or
  `COMPLETE`.
- List genuine Human Gates explicitly. A phase, review, verification, or
  checkpoint label alone is not a Human Gate.
- A current standing milestone covers only its declared exact
  commit/push/tag/publication/readback/named-source-fast-forward/cache/project
  refresh chain without repeat gates.
  Archive, PR, merge, force-push, broad cleanup, dependencies/migrations, and
  unnamed targets remain separate default-deny effects.

